// OVERDUE boss fights, the arena and loot layer. bosses.js holds each boss's character, phases, lines and core; this
// file adds how the fight PLAYS. bosses.js merges it in, so every BOSSES entry carries these fields.
// Inspired by the feel of big looter-shooter boss fights (huge intro, layered health bars, glowing crit spots, a
// loot pinata on death, farmable refights). Every name, mechanic and arena here is original.
//
// SCHEMA: FIGHTS[bossId] = {
//   arena     { name, layout (what it is and where you stand), vertical (the levels and how you get between them),
//               grapple: [grapple points / rails / swing lines], hazards: [{ kind, where, effect }], cover: [{ what, breaks }] }
//             hazard kinds: water | lava | acid | oil | electric | fire | void | gas | rad | paper | crush
//   layers    [{ bar: 'armour' | 'shield' | 'health', of (HP for one player), how (what strips it best) }]  top bar first
//   weakPoints [{ name, glow (what it looks like), exposedBy (what you do to open it), crit (damage multiplier) }]
//   weakness  { element, weapons: [shared/weapons.js ids that are great here], why }. it's always beatable with anything
//             elements: fire | water | shock | frost | slip | verdict | explosive | knockback | blood | sleep | grapple
//   adds      [{ name, count, personality, does }]   minions with their own lines and behaviour
//   twists    [one per phase in bosses.js, in order]  the mechanical twist each phase adds (merged as phases[i].twist)
//   setPiece  [{ kind: 'chase' | 'transform' | 'grapple' | 'vehicle' | 'climb', when, what }]
//   pinata    the death: the burst, the beam, what flies out (an organ core is always guaranteed)
//   lootTable the boss's own LOOT_TABLES id (its dedicated legendaries; farmed on every refight)
//   scaling   how refights scale
//   uses      the mechanics.js ids this fight asks of you (for the coverage table)
// }

